# M3.3 acceptance: the find bar on tests/data/long.pdf (520 US Letter pages, see
# tests/data/make_long_pdf.py). Page n shows the heading "Page n of 520", 25 lines
# "Line i of page n. The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog." and a blue line
# pattern in its lower half. Run from the worktree root with a fresh HOME:
#   mkdir -p /tmp/agentic-reader-m3.3/home
#   scripts/shot.sh -o <repo>/.verify/m3.3/<impl|review> -s tests/acceptance/m3.3.steps -- \
#     env HOME=/tmp/agentic-reader-m3.3/home ./build/app/agentic-reader tests/data/long.pdf
#
# Expected counts (see tests/test_find.cpp, pdftotext as the proxy for Papers): poppler's
# page::search matches substrings, case-insensitive unless Match case is on.
#   "fox"            13000 (25 on every page; counting takes about 30 s with page::search)
#   "520"            546   (every heading, plus "Page 520" and 25 x "of page 520." on page 520)
#   "page 7"         286   (26 on page 7 and on each of pages 70..79)
#   "Page", Match case  520   (the headings only)
#
# Interface choices where the spec is silent:
#   - Ctrl+F shows the bar directly above the PDF pane, in the pane's column, and moves
#     keyboard focus to its text field. The pane loses the bar's height at the top, so
#     every pane y below shifts down by the bar's height (about 35 to 45 px). Ctrl+F
#     works whenever the main window has focus.
#   - The bar holds, left to right: the text field, a "previous" button, a "next"
#     button, a "Match case" checkbox (unchecked at start), the count text and a close
#     button at the right end. Tab order follows that: field, previous, next, Match case,
#     close (the count text takes no focus). Space presses the focused button or toggles
#     the focused checkbox.
#   - The search runs as the text changes (a debounce of at most 150 ms is fine) and
#     again when Match case changes. Each new query cancels the running one.
#   - A new query makes the first match in document order the current match ("1 of N")
#     as soon as it arrives, and scrolls it into view if it is not visible. While the
#     search runs, N grows. The count text is "k of N" (1-based k); its text with no
#     query or no match is the implementation's choice.
#   - Enter in the field or the next button goes to the next match, Shift+Enter or the
#     previous button to the previous one, wrapping at both ends, and scrolls the
#     current match into view when it is not fully visible. Scrolling by hand does not
#     change the current match.
#   - Highlights: every match on the visible pages gets a translucent yellow fill over
#     its rect; the current match gets an orange fill instead. The black text stays
#     readable through both.
#   - Esc in the field and the close button hide the bar, cancel the search and remove
#     every highlight. The view does not scroll when the bar closes.
#
# Geometry without the bar (default 1400x900 window at the screen origin, measured on
# the M3.2 build): menu bar y 0..24, toolbar y 25..66, PDF pane x 225..980 and y
# 67..877. At fit width ("119%") page 1's top edge is at y 79, "Page 1 of 520" at about
# y 145..195, "Line 1 of page 1" at about y 242..256 and "Line 25 of page 1" at about
# y 643..657; the word "fox" on each line is at about x 524..542. A wheel notch scrolls
# 60 px. Page n+1 starts 958 px below page n.
wait 3

# Focus the PDF view.
click 600 500
wait 1

# Start: page 1 of long.pdf at fit width, combo "119%", entry "1 / 520". No find bar,
# nothing highlighted.
shot start

key ctrl+f
wait 1

# Ctrl+F: the find bar is visible above the PDF pane, with an empty text field that has
# keyboard focus (cursor shown), a previous and a next button, an unchecked "Match case"
# checkbox, an empty (or neutral) count text and a close button. The page moved down by
# the bar's height. Nothing is highlighted.
shot bar-open

type fox

# Taken about 0.4 s after the last keystroke (the step pause plus the capture): the
# field reads "fox", the count reads "1 of N" with N at least 25, and every "fox" on
# page 1's 25 lines has a yellow fill except the one on Line 1, which is orange. The
# rest of each line is not highlighted. The UI did not wait for the whole document.
shot typed-fox

wait 1

# About 1.5 s later: still "1 of M" with M larger than N in typed-fox and below 13000:
# the count keeps growing while the search continues. Same highlights as typed-fox.
shot counting

click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
wait 1

# The UI stays responsive during the search: the wheel scrolled the view 600 px down
# while searching. Only the last lines of page 1 remain at the top of the pane, then
# the blue pattern, then page 2's heading "Page 2 of 520" and its first lines. Every
# visible "fox" (page 1's last lines and page 2's lines) is yellow; none is orange (the
# current match on Line 1 of page 1 is above the pane). The count reads "1 of P" with P
# larger than M in counting: the search went on during the scroll. The focus stayed in
# the field.
shot scrolled-while-searching

key Return
wait 1

# Enter: the count reads "2 of ...". The view scrolled back up so that Line 2 of page 1
# is in view; its "fox" is orange. Line 1's "fox" and the other visible ones are yellow.
shot enter-next

key Return
wait 1

# Enter again: "3 of ...", orange on Line 3's "fox" of page 1, Line 2's is yellow now.
# The view did not move (the match was already visible).
shot enter-next-again

key shift+Return
wait 1

# Shift+Enter: back to "2 of ...", orange on Line 2's "fox", Line 3's is yellow again.
shot shift-enter-prev

key Tab Tab space
wait 1

# The next button (focused with two Tabs, pressed with Space): "3 of ...", orange on
# Line 3's "fox".
shot next-button

key shift+Tab space
wait 1

# The previous button: "2 of ...", orange on Line 2's "fox".
shot prev-button

key shift+Tab
key Escape
wait 1

# Esc in the field: the find bar is gone and no highlight is left anywhere. The pane
# is back to its full height (it starts at y 67 again) and page 1's text did not scroll
# apart from moving up by the bar's height.
shot esc-closed

key ctrl+f
key ctrl+a
type 520
wait 10

# Ctrl+F again, "520" typed over any old text. The search has finished: the count reads
# exactly "1 of 546". The "520" of page 1's heading "Page 1 of 520" is orange. No line
# of page 1 contains "520", so nothing else on page 1 is highlighted.
shot 520-done

key Return
wait 1

# Enter: "2 of 546". The view scrolled so that page 2's heading "Page 2 of 520" is in
# view; its "520" is orange. Page 1's heading "520", if still visible, is yellow.
shot 520-next-scrolls

key shift+Return
wait 1

# Shift+Enter: back to "1 of 546", page 1's heading in view with its "520" orange.
shot 520-prev-scrolls

key shift+Return
wait 2

# Shift+Enter on the first match wraps to the last: "546 of 546". The view jumped to
# the end of the document: page 520's lines are in view, and the "520" in "Line 25 of
# page 520." is orange. The "520" in each other visible line of page 520 is yellow.
shot wrap-to-last

key shift+Return
wait 1

# Shift+Enter: "545 of 546", orange moved up one line to "Line 24 of page 520.";
# Line 25's "520" is yellow.
shot last-minus-one

key Return
key Return
wait 2

# Enter twice: to "546 of 546", then wrapping to the first match: "1 of 546". The
# view is back at page 1 with the "520" of "Page 1 of 520" orange.
shot wrap-to-first

key ctrl+a
type page 7
wait 8

# "page 7" (a substring that spans two words, case-insensitive): the count reads exactly
# "1 of 286". The view scrolled to page 7: the "Page 7" of its heading "Page 7 of 520"
# is orange and the "page 7" in each visible line "Line i of page 7." is yellow. The
# numbers before them ("Line i of") are not highlighted.
shot page7-done

key ctrl+a
type Page
wait 2

# "Page" with Match case off: the view is back at page 1. The heading's "Page" is
# orange and the "page" in every line of page 1 is yellow. The count reads "1 of N"
# and is still growing (13520 when done).
shot page-any-case

key Tab Tab Tab space
wait 8

# Match case checked (three Tabs from the field, Space): the old search was cancelled
# and a case-sensitive one ran to the end. The checkbox is checked, the count reads
# exactly "1 of 520", page 1's heading "Page" is orange and no line's "page" is
# highlighted any more.
shot match-case-done

wait 3

# Unchanged: still exactly "1 of 520". No result of the cancelled case-insensitive
# search arrived after the new one started, so the count did not grow and no line's
# "page" turned yellow.
shot match-case-stable

key Tab space
wait 1

# The close button (one Tab from the checkbox, Space): the bar is gone, nothing is
# highlighted, and the pane is back to its full height.
shot close-button
